from langchain_google_genai import ChatGoogleGenerativeAI
from langchain_huggingface import ChatHuggingFace,HuggingFacePipeline
from langchain_core.prompts import PromptTemplate
from langchain_core.output_parsers import StrOutputParser
from dotenv import load_dotenv
from langchain_core.runnables import RunnableParallel
load_dotenv()
model1 = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model = 'gemini-3.6-flash')
llm = HuggingFacePipeline.from_model_id(
model_id = "TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0",
  task="text-generation",
  )
model2 = ChatHuggingFace(llm = llm)
prompt1 = PromptTemplate(template='Generate short and simple notes from the following text {text}',input_variables=['text'])
prompt2 = PromptTemplate(template='Generate 5 questions and answeres from the following text{text}',input_variables=['text'])
prompt3 = PromptTemplate(template='Merge the provided notes and quiz in the single document ->{notes} and {quizes}',input_variables=['notes','quizes'])
parser = StrOutputParser()
parallel_chain = RunnableParallel({
    'notes':prompt1|model1|parser,
    'quizes': prompt2|model2|parser,
})

merge_chain = prompt3|model1|parser
chain = parallel_chain|merge_chain
output = chain.invoke({"""
Web development has become one of the most important fields in the modern technology industry because almost every business, organization, educational institution, and individual now depends on websites and web applications for communication, information, entertainment, and online services. A website is not simply a collection of colorful pages; it is a complete digital environment where different technologies work together to provide users with a smooth and useful experience. HTML, CSS, and JavaScript are considered the fundamental technologies of front-end web development, and each one has a different but equally important responsibility. HTML, which stands for HyperText Markup Language, is used to create the basic structure of a webpage. It allows developers to add headings, paragraphs, images, links, buttons, forms, tables, lists, and many other elements to a webpage. Without HTML, a browser would not have a proper structure to display the content. CSS, or Cascading Style Sheets, is responsible for the visual appearance of a website. With CSS, developers can change colors, fonts, backgrounds, borders, spacing, alignment, width, height, and positioning of different elements. CSS also allows developers to create responsive designs that can automatically adjust according to different screen sizes, such as mobile phones, tablets, laptops, and desktop computers. JavaScript adds functionality and interactivity to websites. For example, JavaScript can be used to create interactive buttons, form validation, image sliders, navigation menus, pop-up messages, calculators, animations, search features, and dynamic content. When these three technologies are combined properly, developers can create modern, attractive, responsive, and interactive websites. In addition to these basic technologies, modern web development also includes frameworks, libraries, databases, APIs, backend technologies, authentication systems, cloud services, and deployment platforms. Front-end developers may use technologies such as React, Angular, Vue, or Next.js to build complex user interfaces, while backend developers may use Node.js, Python, Java, PHP, or other programming languages to handle server-side operations. Databases such as MongoDB, MySQL, PostgreSQL, and Firebase can be used to store and manage application data. APIs allow different applications and services to communicate with each other and exchange information. For example, a weather application can use an API to receive current weather information from a remote server and display it to the user. Modern websites also need to consider important factors such as performance, accessibility, security, search engine optimization, and user experience. A website that looks beautiful but loads very slowly may not provide a good experience, while a fast website that is difficult to navigate can also frustrate users. Security is another major concern because websites often handle sensitive information such as usernames, passwords, personal information, and payment details. Developers therefore need to follow secure coding practices, validate user input, protect authentication systems, and properly manage access to data. Responsive design has also become extremely important because users access websites from many different devices and screen sizes. A professional developer should therefore understand how layouts behave on different screens and use techniques such as Flexbox, CSS Grid, media queries, and relative units to create flexible designs. Learning web development is not only about memorizing syntax; it is about understanding how different concepts work together and using them to solve real-world problems. Beginners often start by learning HTML elements and document structure, then move toward CSS styling and layout techniques, and finally learn JavaScript programming and browser interaction. After becoming comfortable with these fundamentals, they can explore frameworks, backend development, databases, APIs, authentication, cloud computing, and artificial intelligence. Practical projects are one of the best ways to improve web development skills because projects allow learners to apply theoretical concepts to real problems. A beginner can start with simple projects such as a personal portfolio, login page, calculator, to-do application, landing page, or weather application and gradually move toward larger projects such as e-commerce websites, learning management systems, social media applications, or AI-powered web applications. The field of web development is continuously evolving, and new tools and technologies are introduced regularly. However, the fundamental concepts of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, programming logic, problem solving, and software architecture remain extremely valuable. A developer who understands these fundamentals can learn new frameworks and technologies more easily because they understand the principles behind them rather than depending completely on ready-made code. Therefore, web development can be considered a combination of creativity, programming, problem solving, and continuous learning. It provides developers with the ability to transform ideas into useful digital products that can be accessed by people around the world. With consistent practice, patience, and a willingness to understand concepts deeply, anyone interested in technology can gradually develop the skills required to build professional websites and modern web applications.

"""})
print(output)


